<h1 class="mt-3">How It Works</h1>
<p class="text-muted" style="font-size:14px;">Getting started on Local Connect</p>

<h2>1. Register an account</h2>
<p>Choose your role when signing up — Citizen, Organization, or Community Admin. Each role has a different level of
    access and responsibility on the platform.</p>

<h2>2. Verify your email (Citizens)</h2>
<p>After registering, citizens receive a verification email. Click the link to activate your account and log in.</p>

<h2>3. Submit for review (Organizations & Community Admins)</h2>
<p>Organizations and community admins upload a verification document during registration. A system admin reviews the
    submission and approves trusted accounts before they can post.</p>

<h2>4. Complete your profile</h2>
<p>Approved organizations and community admins complete their public profile — adding a bio, contact details, and
    profile image — before accessing the platform.</p>

<h2>5. Create and share posts</h2>
<p>Verified pages can create posts: alerts, events, volunteer opportunities, notices, training sessions, and community
    updates. Posts appear in the home feed for all users.</p>

<h2>6. Citizens engage</h2>
<p>Citizens can follow organizations, save posts, like and comment, sign up to volunteer, view local alerts on a map,
    and report harmful content.</p>

<h2>7. Stay informed</h2>
<p>Receive in-app notifications when organizations you follow post new content, when your volunteer status changes, or
    when important alerts are posted in your area.</p>